        "id": 106141,
        "name": "Ameena",
        "username": "Ameena",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/{size}/1907_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-06-11T20:16:40.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Lol what was it, Backlash Fields? Those are nasty (I think he has two in total). The Living Forcefields can be annoying if you only have low-damage heroes (such as Tachyon).</p><p>Worst card for me, though, has to be Devious Disruption. Yeah it's a one-shot rather than an ongoing but that card has been the cause of more of our defeats than probably anything else in Blade's deck. The amount of times we've had it come up thrice in a game is ridiculous - there are only two copies, but on more than one occasion we've had both in the trash when Blade has flipped, meaning they get shuffled back into the deck for one of them to come out shortly afterwards and finish us off (or near enough that something else can then finish the job). We've had Blade flip and then take no damage before we all die horribly as well...more than once :P.</p>",
        "post_number": 4,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:35:58.210Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
